course: dictionary
lesson: 14569
title: Pigmentation: the colour of living things
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Pigmentation is a long word, but its root is pigment, a coloured substance. Pigmentation is the natural colour that a living thing has, caused by these pigments. The ending -ation shows a process or result, so think of it as the colour that comes from pigments.
explain: Use the context to check. «Her skin has a warm brown pigmentation, which comes from melanin.» The words natural, skin and melanin all point to colour, not a rash or a bruise, so pigmentation must mean the colour of skin.
explain: The word can also mean coloured spots or patches on skin. «The doctor looked at the brown pigmentation on his arm and said it was harmless.» Ask yourself: does the sentence still make sense if I swap in colour or patches? If it does, you have the right meaning.
explain: Scientists use pigmentation for plants and animals too. «The leaves have green pigmentation from chlorophyll.» Pigmentation is never a sign that someone is better or worse than anyone else.
fact: Pigmentation means the natural colour of skin, hair, eyes, leaves or other living things.
fact: A pigment is a coloured substance. Melanin is the pigment that gives skin, hair and eyes their colour.
fact: More melanin means darker skin. «Pigmentation» can also mean coloured spots or patches on skin.
fact: Animals' pigmentation can help them hide, which is called camouflage.
fact: Differences in skin pigmentation are natural and say nothing about a person's worth.
exercise: «Her hair has a deep red pigmentation that shines in the sun.» What does pigmentation mean here? | A sore, itchy rash | A type of hair brush | *The natural colour of her hair | A sudden cold wind
exercise: «The leaves turn yellow in autumn as their green pigmentation fades.» What causes the green pigmentation in leaves? | Tiny holes in the leaves | The weight of the leaves | The wind blowing them down | *Pigments, such as chlorophyll, in the leaves
exercise: «The nurse said the small brown pigmentation on Sam's cheek was normal.» Find and copy the one word that means the coloured patch on skin. | *pigmentation | nurse | small | normal
test: Melanin is a pigment. What does more melanin usually mean? | Bigger eyes | Thinner hair | Lighter skin | *Darker skin
test: Why is pigmentation not a sign of a person's worth? | Darker skin means someone is better | Pigmentation only happens to animals | Lighter skin means someone is cleverer | *Skin colour is natural and differs between people, so it says nothing about worth
exam: Which sentence uses pigmentation to mean coloured patches on skin? | «The sun made the air feel warm.» | «She painted a picture of the sea.» | *«The doctor noticed a patch of pigmentation on the baby's back, which was harmless.» | «The bus was late again.»
